 VALUES ('a1af9fd5-6a98-5c4c-9778-230878cb4227', 91, '249f74c7-cc2c-5c23-b6c8-1d896bb97022',
         'Node.js Basics', 'Basics Node.js', 'Node.js',
         'Run a basic Node.js script, understand the REPL, and module system (require/export).', 'Run a basic Node.js script, understand the REPL, and module system (require/export).',
         'Node.js brings JavaScript to the server. The REPL lets you evaluate expressions interactively. Every file is a module, and module.exports exposes public API. CommonJS (require) is the default until ES modules are configured. Understanding the module lifecycle (load -> evaluate -> export) is the foundation for everything that follows.', 'Node.js brings JavaScript to the server. The REPL lets you evaluate expressions interactively. Every file is a module, and module.exports exposes public API. CommonJS (require) is the default until ES modules are configured. Understanding the module lifecycle (load -> evaluate -> export) is the foundation for everything that follows.', 90,
         'Write a small Node.js app that exports a add(a, b) function and calls it from a separate script.', 'Write a small Node.js app that exports a add(a, b) function and calls it from a separate script.',
         'Two files: a module and a script that imports and uses it.', 'Two files: a module and a script that imports and uses it.',
         ARRAY['Module file uses module.exports', 'Importing script runs without errors']::text[], ARRAY['Module file uses module.exports', 'Importing script runs without errors']::text[],
         'Create a module that exports an HTTP server on port 3000 and returns Hello on the root path.', 'Create a module that exports an HTTP server on port 3000 and returns Hello on the root path.',
         '{}'::text[], 'lesson')
