 VALUES ('031c02d7-b61c-58dd-96e8-186d68aaee7c', 92, '249f74c7-cc2c-5c23-b6c8-1d896bb97022',
         'HTTP and the Request-Response Cycle', 'HTTP and the Request-Response Cycle', 'HTTP',
         'Explain methods, status codes, headers, and the difference between GET and POST.', 'Explain methods, status codes, headers, and the difference between GET and POST.',
         'HTTP is the language of the web. GET retrieves a representation; POST submits data for processing. Status codes in the 2xx range signal success, 4xx signal client errors, and 5xx signal server errors. Headers carry metadata (content type, authentication, caching). Every response should set a meaningful content-type header.', 'HTTP is the language of the web. GET retrieves a representation; POST submits data for processing. Status codes in the 2xx range signal success, 4xx signal client errors, and 5xx signal server errors. Headers carry metadata (content type, authentication, caching). Every response should set a meaningful content-type header.', 90,
         'Use curl to test a local Node.js server for successful and error status codes.', 'Use curl to test a local Node.js server for successful and error status codes.',
         'A text file listing the status codes you observed and what they mean.', 'A text file listing the status codes you observed and what they mean.',
         ARRAY['Can distinguish GET from POST', 'Can explain what a 404 status code means']::text[], ARRAY['Can distinguish GET from POST', 'Can explain what a 404 status code means']::text[],
         'Write a brief client-side note comparing GET vs POST for submitting a form.', 'Write a brief client-side note comparing GET vs POST for submitting a form.',
         ARRAY['91']::text[], 'lesson')
