 VALUES ('a7b2fb63-4133-5d8a-a62b-fee6d4d1be21', 93, '249f74c7-cc2c-5c23-b6c8-1d896bb97022',
         'Intro to Express', 'Intro to Express', 'Express',
         'Set up an Express server, define a route, and listen on a port.', 'Set up an Express server, define a route, and listen on a port.',
         'Express is the de-facto web framework for Node.js. app.listen(port) starts the server, app.METHOD(path, handler) defines routes. Middleware functions (req, res, next) have access to the request and response objects and the next middleware function in the application''s request-processing cycle. "Hello, world" is the traditional first Express app.', 'Express is the de-facto web framework for Node.js. app.listen(port) starts the server, app.METHOD(path, handler) defines routes. Middleware functions (req, res, next) have access to the request and response objects and the next middleware function in the application''s request-processing cycle. "Hello, world" is the traditional first Express app.', 100,
         'Start an Express server that responds JSON {"status":"ok"} on /health.', 'Start an Express server that responds JSON {"status":"ok"} on /health.',
         'A running Express server with at least two routes.', 'A running Express server with at least two routes.',
         ARRAY['Server starts without crashing', 'Two routes are registered']::text[], ARRAY['Server starts without crashing', 'Two routes are registered']::text[],
         'Add a route that logs the request method and URL, then responds with "received".', 'Add a route that logs the request method and URL, then responds with "received".',
         ARRAY['92']::text[], 'practice')
